        "id": "ch2_5-1",
        "text": "User Input\nAnother way to interact with the supplied input from the shell script is to use\nthe read function. Again, the best way to explain this is through examples. We\nwill ask the user to enter their first name and last name after which we will\nprint the full name on the screen:\n#!/bin/bash\nread -p \"Please enter your first name:\" FIRSTNAME\nread -p \"Please enter your last name:\" LASTNAME\nprintf \"Your full name is: $FIRSTNAME $LASTNAME\\n\"\nTo execute it, we just enter the script name (we don\u2019t need to supply any\nparameters like we did before). Once we enter the script\u2019s name, we will be\nprompted with the messages defined in the previous script:\nroot@kali:~# nameprint.sh\nPlease enter your first name:Gus\nPlease enter your last name:Khawaja\nYour full name is: Gus Khawaja",
